{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$Z \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$Z \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to Z$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-universally-injective-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8f136fd6b95038bc0e525c7717f53eea0d34eba36d14f519157f4fa68504e3f4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9632a6185dc506cee4b8bef55a9a378003d50a6bde9a7c73255d038fa007a6fa", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is universally injective,\n<STRUCT_0003> for every affine scheme <MATH_0003> and any morphism\n<MATH_0004> the morphism <MATH_0005>\nis universally injective, and\n<STRUCT_0004> add more here.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:035543a9d2a40917908eddac21234bbde70a219d999da84aeccf1e8d1b3bcff6", "unit_id": "tag:0DTN:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$g : V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_g$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta_g$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0009": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Delta_f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b07fa7652a393ae291a10c0c988ebbeb77cecd7eabc922fbb2787c70b5ffe81f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e015f016943b10acd3c414d415c3f9ece0ecb0e36d4b6be16ed42f8c1cb17c63", "source_text": "The implication (1) <MATH_0001> (2) is immediate.\nAssume (2) holds. We will show that\n<MATH_0002>\nis surjective, which implies (1) by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nConsider an affine scheme <MATH_0003> and a smooth morphism\n<MATH_0004>. Since\n<MATH_0005>\nis universally injective by (2), we see that\n<MATH_0006> is surjective.\nHowever, <MATH_0007> is the base change of <MATH_0008>\nby the smooth morphism <MATH_0009>.\nSince the collection of these morphisms <MATH_0010>\nare jointly surjective, we conclude <MATH_0011> is surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8726249538253b6bcf9c7e0456fd515e7c8f9a611919065210180bd1c8492455", "unit_id": "tag:0DTN:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$W$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-universally-injective-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87955b6b44be14f27ae02579c55634c9110a1b1232924689b9913f16226d9a28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:216026a863504e95e39a63b671be2e665fed56c4abe4cc236d3e31aaa139b1ca", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation where <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space. If the base change\n<MATH_0004> is universally injective,\nthen <MATH_0005> is universally injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1d5a4fc1ab16044441f1eee2729389162ef842da6fad3daf00f830055b1366cc", "unit_id": "tag:0DTP:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta_g$", "MATH_0002": "$g : W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_g$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-check-property-covering}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d7eb673e3a9ebca1b124322f2105ebe297cdce785c880c9f8537879f9fa5db13", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e549e60d26801ddc2a9a63e28795dcf279f63d1940f99da3ba747a83c97d7712", "source_text": "Observe that the diagonal <MATH_0001> of the morphism\n<MATH_0002>\nis the base change of <MATH_0003> by <MATH_0004>.\nHence if <MATH_0005> is surjective, then so is <MATH_0006>\nby Properties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nThus the lemma follows from the characterization (2)\nin Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:86a09b27cffa1b3ed9e1c839ed1cb4477ec8221d1f92cb337f37f9791640c042", "unit_id": "tag:0DTP:proof"}
